Job Description:
Job Description
Our Trade Mark Enforcement Department has a vacant position for a qualified Attorney. We are looking for a young, energetic and highly driven candidate to become part of this well-established and growing practice. The ideal candidate is confident with excellent written and oral communication abilities, ability to handle multiple priorities, and a good understanding of client needs. If you enjoy trade mark litigation and anti-counterfeiting enforcement work including training, search and seizure operations, and multi-jurisdictional matters and have the desire to take your career to the next level, then this is for you. This role represents a great opportunity within a challenging and professional environment.
Key responsibilities of the Trade Mark Senior Associate will include, but not limited to:
Drafting legal documents i.e. opinions, contracts, agreements, letters of demand and articles;
Monthly invoicing of fees and disbursements;
Compilation of quotes;
File and document management (uploading documents, correspondences, managing/ monitoring deadlines, court online processes);
Liaising with clients and agents;
Attending consultations with council;
Day to day running of trade mark litigation and Anti-Counterfeiting practice.
Arranging and delivering brand identification training seminars to Customs and Police authorities across Africa;
Coordinating and participating in search and seizure operations to defend clients’ intellectual property rights in countries such as Benin, Botswana, Cameroon, Ethiopia, Ghana, Ivory Coast, Kenya, Mozambique, Nigeria, South Africa, Tanzania, Uganda, Zambia, and Zimbabwe;
Following up on enforcement actions with rigorous civil and criminal litigation in relation to anti-counterfeiting.
Minimum requirements:
Completed LLB with 2 years of Clerkship served in an IP firm;
Admitted Attorney;
Knowledge and understanding of Trade Marks is essential as is completion of the trade mark practitioner’s examination;
Experience in and ability to do legal research and draft opinions;
Fully computer literate on MS Office (Knowledge Patricia and Elite 3E will be advantageous);
Excellent written & oral communication skills and good command of English;
Must be able to multi-task;
Able to work independently;
Deadline driven;
Good team player;
Good interpersonal skills;
Personal development abilities;
Client focused;
Good negotiation skills;
Able to maintain an orderly working environment;
Punctual and reliable;
Good work ethics.

The CSIR has a vacancy for a Principal Researcher: Computer Vision in the Optronic Sensor Systems Impact Area, within the Defence and Security cluster. The incumbent will assist to drive strategic direction for innovation in digital optronics research and applications, which focuses on computer vision applications integrating over physics and system performance modelling and simulation, algorithm development, sensor/systems integration, deployment, test and evaluation (T&E). . This is based in Pretoria and will report to the Research Group Leader.
Key responsibilities:
Technical Expertise
Create, refine and implement new computer vision systems in a variety of applications including security, mining, manufacturing, and remote sensing;
Design and implement superior solutions and differentiated products/systems;
Lead the analysis and implementation from physics and end-user requirements to integrate solutions to create video surveillance/monitoring/intelligence user systems for deployment and evaluation;
Develop end-user computer vision applications while integrating active and passive sensors, visual and non-visual spectrum, LIDAR sensors, optical and non-optical elements;
Drive the implementation of video analytics based on human behaviour analysis;
Conduct research on technologies to improve team and systems innovation, processes, and productivity.
Knowledge Generation and Dissemination
Strategically develop a computer vision research and applications program to support doctoral and masters' students, journal publications, and international visibility;
Publish papers in peer-reviewed journals or book chapters, or editor of book/conference proceedings;
Lead and contribute to the development of new and adapted technologies for licencing, patenting and transfer to new and existing industries;
Contribute to the development of policies and procedures.
Human Capital Development
Strategically develop human capital resources to ensure succession and skills transfer within the modelling, simulation, and radiometric domain;
Strategically create human capital development pipelines through industry and university collaboration;
Lead in developing researchers and co-supervision of students;
Contribute in the development, mentoring, and coaching of the team
Contribute in attracting, developing, and retaining talent.
Research Leadership
Lead and support engagements across public, private and international stakeholders;
Formulate national and international Research and Development (R&D) strategies in collaboration with various partners;
Serve on national and international research working groups / advisory boards / editorial boards;
Provide thought leadership, drive business growth within the market, and develop and maintain client relationships;
Create international awareness and partnerships for CSIR digital optronics research capabilities.
Attracting Funding
Develop strategic R&D relationships at national and international scale;
Create commercialization opportunities for through industry engagement locally and internationally;
Source and manage large interdisciplinary projects / programmes;
Attract sufficient funds for large teams of researchers and support staff;
Write proposals and project definitions and research business plans.
Project Resource Management
Generate and update work breakdown structures (WBS) and statement of works (SOW);
Plan projects with team members (quality and completeness of project management plan including project scope, schedule, cost budget, risk analysis);
Lead and deliver the technical deliverables that are necessary for the design, optimization, and/or commercialization of products/outputs;
Lead and execute project technical deliverables and milestones to ensure successful delivery of new processes and/or products;
Perform quality assurance, code review, code refactoring, and maintenance on radiometric modelling and simulation software;
Compile research findings, reports, and other documentation(s), for both internal and external stakeholders.
Qualifications, skills and experience:
A Master's degree in computer science, electronic/mechanical/mechatronic/computer engineering, applied mathematics, physics or related fields with at least eight years' experience in the following:
Research and development environment, defining product application strategy, establishing client relationships, soliciting user requirements and delivering innovative solutions;
Computer vision, sensors, electro-optics and infrared sensors systems integration and product development environment, with strong user system application development.
Must have experience in the following:
Computer Vision technology and product development;
Electro-optic system modelling and simulation.
Must have track record in the following:
Development of video surveillance/monitoring/intelligence user application systems, including video analytics development;
Developing research, development and innovation capabilities;
Product/solutions development;
Leadership, mentorship and guidance of team members;
Publications in high-impact journals.
Must be able to:
Integrate over many fields including radiometry, optronic systems applications, sensors, cameras, and computer vision;
Operate at user application level for deep understanding of user needs.
