Job Description:
Transport Education Training Authority is looking to fill the role of Accountant for the duration till June 2026
Job Description
KEY PERFORMANCE AREAS
Financial Reporting and Compliance
Prepare monthly, quarterly, and annual financial statements in accordance with GRAP and PFMA;
Ensure timely submission of reports to the Auditor-General, National Treasury, and DHET;
Maintain accurate general ledger accounts including Annual Financial Statements and perform reconciliations;
Assist with the preparation of audit files and respond to audit queries.
Budgeting and Forecasting
Support the Finance Manager in compiling annual budgets and forecasts;
Monitor budget performance and provide variance analysis;
Prepare the reallocation of budgets per chamber/implementing business unit based on project performance and strategic priorities.
Prepare Quarterly reports to DHET, National Treasury and review of the medium term expenditure framework , and ENEs.
Grant Management
Monitor financial transactions related to Discretionary and Mandatory Grants;
Reconcile grant expenditure against approved allocations;
Ensure compliance with grant funding policies and procedures;
Liaise with stakeholders on financial aspects of non-pivotal programmes.
Ensure reconciliations monthly DG expenditure reconciliations with the Chambers and Implementing units to a specific financial year applicable.
Ensure timeous processing of DG and MG payments when the claims have been received.
Internal Controls and Risk Management
Implement and maintain financial controls to safeguard SETA assets;
Identify and mitigate financial risks;
Ensure compliance with internal policies and procedures.
Stakeholder Engagement
Collaborate with implementing units/chambers, oversight committees, internal and external auditors;
Provide financial support and guidance to project managers and grant recipients;
Participate in finance-related workshops and stakeholder engagements.
Systems and Process Improvement
Support the integration of financial systems with project management tools;
Recommend improvements to financial processes and reporting mechanisms.
Job Requirements
MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS
Qualification and Experience
Minimum of a BCom Degree (NQFL 7) qualification majoring in Accounting or equivalent.
A Postgraduate qualification is an added advantage;
Completed SAICA articles will be an added advantage
Minimum 5 years’ experience in financial accounting, preferably in the public sector or SETA environment;
Knowledge of PFMA, GRAP, Treasury Regulations, and SETA grant frameworks.
Knowledge and Skills
Knowledge and Understanding of:
Business Administration knowledge;
Proficiency in financial systems (e.g, SAGE X3, or any ERP systems);
GRAP and IFRS;
Advanced Excel skills.
Skills
Administrative;
Customer services;
Problem solving;
Excellent communication and facilitation skills;
Facilitating skills;
Problem solving.

Description
Welcome and assist all visitors and employees in a professional and courteous manner;
Operate the switchboard by efficiently receiving, screening, and directing incoming calls to the appropriate departments;
Maintain a clean, organised, and professional reception area that reflects the company’s image and service standards;
Coordinate outgoing deliveries and courier collections to ensure efficient communication flow;
Create and issue access permits in accordance with FlySafair and ACSA security procedures;
Facilitate the end-to-end ACSA permit application and renewal process for employees and contractors;
Facilitate the issuing of crew cards to new and existing employees;
Monitor upcoming permit expiries and perform timely reprints and distribution to all bases;
Liaise with ACSA offices and internal departments to coordinate documentation, appointments, and approvals;
Provide front-desk assistance and respond to queries related to access permits;
Maintain and update the employee access permit database, ensuring all personnel details, photographs, access levels, and expiry dates are accurately recorded and kept current;
Monitor and update the company vehicle logbook, ensuring accuracy and compliance with usage policies;
Monitor the scheduling and administration of company car wash services;
Provide general administrative support to the HR & Corporate Services team as required.
Requirements
Grade 12 or Equivalent (Essential).
Certificate or Diploma in Office Administration or related field (Advantageous).
1–2 years’ experience in a reception, front-office, Helpdesk or administrative support role (Essential).
Experience within an Aviation, Corporate, or Customer-Service environment (Advantageous).
Exposure to switchboard operations, visitor management systems, or access control processes (Advantageous).
Personal Attributes:
Professional, courteous, and approachable demeanour.
High integrity.
Reliable and dependable.
Positive attitude with a strong sense of responsibility.
Team-oriented with a service-driven mindset
